    html: `${breadcrumb([{ label: "Youth safety" }])}${internalHero("Youth safety", "Career exploration should use clear boundaries.", "These expectations apply when students use the program, contact Navio, or plan a conversation or experience test involving another person.")}
    <section class="section"><div class="container narrow policy-copy"><h2>Public program</h2><p>The program and workbook require no account and do not submit a student's written answers to Navio. Students should keep personal reflections private and avoid placing sensitive information in messages.</p><h2>Professional conversations</h2><p>Use public or appropriately supervised communication. Involve a parent, guardian, educator, or trusted adult where appropriate. A student should never feel pressured to share private contact details, move to an unexpected account, meet alone, accept an offer, or disclose personal information.</p><h2>Experience tests</h2><p>Choose a safe, age-appropriate scope. A volunteer task, observation, visit, or conversation should follow the responsible school, organization, workplace, and parent or guardian requirements.</p><h2>Organization communication</h2><p>Navio uses its public email and official social profiles. Career learning does not include unapproved private mentoring, recruitment, employment, or private contact between a student and a contributor.</p><h2>Report a concern</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:${email}?subject=Youth%20safety%20concern">${email}</a> with “Youth safety concern” in the subject line. Include what happened, when, the activity involved, and a safe way to respond. Email is not an emergency channel; contact local emergency services if someone is in immediate danger.</p>${reviewed}</div></section>`,
